{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>My wife bore me.</b> It would have been fitting for him to say 'Rachel bore,' but the matter is that he did not take a wife of his own will except Rachel alone, and therefore he says of her 'my wife' — meaning that no children were born to me from a wife who is my wife by my choice except two, and I have placed my love upon them as though they were only sons, and the rest are to me like sons of concubines. And this is why Scripture everywhere gives precedence to Rachel over Leah, as it says (Ruth 4): ״כרחל וכלאה אשר בנו שתיהן את בית ישראל״, and (Genesis 31): ״ויקרא לרחל וללאה השדה״ — for the principal pillar of the house was Rachel. And in this parashah it is written ״בני רחל אשת יעקב״, but of Leah Scripture did not use such an expression. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:15.080658942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}